Karate Kid: Legends is a 2025 American martial arts drama film starring Jackie
Chan and Ralph Macchio, while introducing Ben Wang as the main lead.

14
00:50:36,923 --> 00:50:42,923
It is the sixth film in The Karate Kid franchise, serving as a follow-up to The
Karate Kid (2010) and the television series Cobra Kai (2018–2025).

15
00:54:13,846 --> 00:54:19,846
Both Chan and Macchio reprise their roles from the franchise—the latter's first
involvement in a film from the franchise since The Karate Kid Part III (1989).

16
00:57:50,769 --> 00:57:56,769
The story follows Li (Wang), a kung fu prodigy who, after moving to New York and
confronting a local karate champion, receives help from his former master Mr.

17
01:01:27,692 --> 01:01:33,692
Han (Chan) and karate sensei Daniel LaRusso (Macchio).

18
01:05:04,615 --> 01:05:10,615
It is the first film in the series not to be produced
by Jerry Weintraub, who died in 2015.

19
01:08:41,538 --> 01:08:47,538
The film was confirmed to be in development in September 2022, with Jonathan Entwistle
set to direct and Rob Lieber set to write the screenplay in November 2023.

20
01:12:18,461 --> 01:12:24,461
Casting took place from November 2023 to April 2024.

21
01:15:55,384 --> 01:16:01,384
Principal photography took place from April to June 2024.

22
01:19:32,307 --> 01:19:38,307
Karate Kid: Legends premiered at the Cinépolis Mitikah in Mexico City, Mexico on May 7, 2025,
and was released in the United States by Sony Pictures Releasing on May 30.

23
01:23:09,230 --> 01:23:15,230
It received mixed reviews from critics and has grossed $117 million worldwide.

24
01:26:46,153 --> 01:26:52,153
